{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338575-brainstorming-an-artifact-\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022-suit-of-armor","id":1338575,"title":"Brainstorming an Artifact \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 suit of armor","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-09-29T23:11:22-07:00","id":1338575,"title":"Brainstorming an Artifact \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 suit of armor","content":"First off: holy crap I'm actually going to run Exalted!<br /> <br /> One of my players asked permission for a five-dot Artifact, and I granted it because it gives me a plot hook. The character is a Dynast's former retainer, who became a Dawn caste when he killed something he shouldn't have been able to kill (haven't settled on exactly what, yet). The Artifact is something he stole as he was fleeing the Dynast's service (the Dynast in question isn't a canon character, but I know who she is).<br /> <br /> The character is going for the &quot;immovable object&quot; theme in combat, and the player and I settled on a suit of armor as his Artifact. I'm thinking white jade articulated plate, with mostly defensive Evocations.<br /> <br /> Diamond Clarity<br /> Cost: TBD Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Perilous<br /> Duration: Scene<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> <br /> &lt;Armor name&gt; lends its wearer's mind the clarity of a flawless diamond. She gains &lt;Essence&gt; automatic successes on Integrity rolls to resist both social and magical mental influence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1856-hakkonen","name":"Hakkonen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T00:07:33-07:00","id":1338577,"title":"","content":"Quick question - have you read <i>Arms of the Chosen</i>?<br /> <br /> \u200bOne thing I'd keep in mind when homebrewing Artifact weapons and armor is that the dot rating doesn't just reflect the power level of the artifact and its Evocations; it also covers its potential to impact both the battlefield as a whole and the fighting style of the player character.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe Distaff (an Artifact 3 blunted daiklave) has Evocations that let you make Disarm and Grapple attempts more easily, and can weave little people-shapes out of silk to assist you with Craft or Medicine actions; by contrast, the Forgotten Blade (an Artifact 5 daiklave) lets you carve memories out of people <i>as a baseline</i> and can eventually turn you into a bladed storm of amnesia, leaving behind armies of corpses that will never be recognized.<br /> <br /> \u200bLikewise, for armor, there's Baldaquin (an artifact 3 lamellar artifact), whose Evocations improve the wearer's diplomatic capabilities, while Mela's Coil (an Artifact 5 articulated plate) makes you a razor-clawed constrictor right out of the box, and whose capstone involves turning into a dragon.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T00:34:32-07:00","id":1338584,"title":"","content":"(Also for some reason I get an error message when I try and view this thread; I suspect it has to do with my laptop's browser having difficulty with the special characters used in the thread title. It works fine from my cell phone though.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T00:56:09-07:00","id":1338586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338575-brainstorming-an-artifact-\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022-suit-of-armor?p=1338577#post1338577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick question - have you read <i>Arms of the Chosen</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have not, but now I think I should. The Forgotten Blade and Mela's Coil both sound much weirder than I was considering going for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1856-hakkonen","name":"Hakkonen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T03:33:07-07:00","id":1338593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hakkonen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338575-brainstorming-an-artifact-\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022-suit-of-armor?p=1338586#post1338586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have not, but now I think I should. The Forgotten Blade and Mela's Coil both sound much weirder than I was considering going for.</div> </div> </div> </div>It helps to start with a strong theme from which to start - Mela's Coil is a blue jade banded armor whose theme is centered around making the wearer express the elemental fury of the air dragon for whom it is named.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe blade Volcano Cutter is centered around building up the explosive pressure of a volcanic eruption and unleashing it against an enemy that <i>needs</i> that sheer level of overkill to deal with.<br /> <br /> The black armor Five Edicts Dominion wants its wearer to be the threatening dark lord to whom even the mighty must kneel, one whose heart fills with contempt for his fellow man and seeks out bargains with dead gods.<br /> <br /> The armor Unison is almost a living thing, treating its wearer more like a host it must protect, shifting itself to better serve until the line between them blurs..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 09-30-2019, 06:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T06:10:31-07:00","id":1338609,"title":"","content":"Some ideas :<br /> <br /> -<b>Virtue's Call :</b> An armor of shining White Jade which holds an intimacy of your choice as sacred. All actions to uphold and further that Intimacy are greatly enhanced, however going against this Intimacy has equally dire consequences for the wearer.<br /> <br /> -<b>Aeons' Embrace :</b> A Starmetal armor which looks older than Creation itself, regal yet always giving the feeling that it's about to fall apart. Slows down everything around the wearer, dulling blows and creating opportunities to strike back where none exist. The armor seeks to create a moment of perfect clarity in which the wearer may unleash the perfect strike. Careless wearers are known to fall under the armor's influence, gradually becoming slower and more detached in all things.<br /> <br /> -<b>Heart of the Grove :</b> A Green Jade armor worn by the defenders of a sacred forest. Literally roots the user, anchoring them to the ground with vines of Essence to repel blows and draw strength from the earth. The Armor's true wish is to spread nature's beauty throughout the world, and as such its stronger Evocations may leave budding groves behind. Note : aforementioned defenders of the sacred forest probably want it back badly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T06:36:03-07:00","id":1338611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hakkonen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338575-brainstorming-an-artifact-\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022-suit-of-armor?p=1338586#post1338586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have not, but now I think I should. The Forgotten Blade and Mela's Coil both sound much weirder than I was considering going for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those ones are, but it's not intrinsic to what five dot Artifacts are. There's a lot of versatility in what each dot level can cover; three dots ranges from the comparatively simple Spring Razor to the intelligent and magic cleaving Beloved Adorei.<br /> <br /> I can definitely see your concept of becoming a diamond-hard pillar working. Although suddenly I'm imagining the cap Charm being something mythically evocative like hardening into a turtle stele or jizo statue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T07:21:43-07:00","id":1338624,"title":"","content":"Think less &quot;must be weird&quot; and more &quot;Artifact 5 enable new playstyles in very large scale ways&quot;, so to speak. Death at the Root enables manse destruction, hearthstone destruction and recreation, Sorcerous Working destruction or stasis, and so on, while Weirdflame allows you to fire mutagenic Essence into people. Though there are some not-so-good examples of them on the armor side, like Seven Furies Caged or Unison, that don't really manage to enable new playstyles as much as they just enhance existing playstyles strongly. <br /> <br /> (Also, btw, you don't roll Integrity for influence; you apply influence against a static Resolve value, and having +(Essence) Resolve against everything as a passive bonus is too much, personally)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T07:46:01-07:00","id":1338628,"title":"","content":"The three big things, in my opinion, when thinking about an artifact 5 are scope, style, and legend.<br /> <br /> The first one, scope, increasing as you go from 3 to 5 dots means less that evocations become more and more powerful, and more that they become wider and grander in scope. So an artifact 3 weapon might fire a lightning bolt while an artifact 5 conjures an entire thunderstorm. Mechanically that lightning bolt may actually seal more damage and be technically more optimal for single combat, but that typhoon can wipe out the entire docks ward of a city, if not the entire thing. It doesn\u2019t necessarily have to scale up to city destroying stuff in scale, but they tend not to just go crazy with mechanical numbers effects. Like that immovable armor is way more likely to unleash a point blank earthquake that knocks down everyone but the user out to four range bands than it is to have a scenelong charm that adds 25 soak or something.<br /> <br /> The next, as mentioned above, is style. A lot of artifact 5 weapons and armor are almost like martial arts unto themselves. I don\u2019t think there\u2019s any that I\u2019d say you don\u2019t even need any native combat charms for, but there\u2019s a few where if you took every evocation and a like number of native charms you\u2019d be JUST fine. They also tend towards not being super omni-applicable. Like instead of adding dice to all attacks they only add to a certain gambit, or only in certain situations that make sense in theme. Generally just flat \u201cgain bonuses to this roll in all circumstances.\u201d Are the purview if native charms. Reading Arms of the Chosen will give you a much better idea of this. <br /> <br /> Lastly legend. Artifact 5s should be, probably, a big part of your PCs legend. As much as King Arthur and Thor are related to their weapons. So it should be a pretty big deal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T05:30:32-07:00","id":1338767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338575-brainstorming-an-artifact-\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022-suit-of-armor?p=1338593#post1338593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It helps to start with a strong theme from which to start - Mela's Coil is a blue jade banded armor whose theme is centered around making the wearer express the elemental fury of the air dragon for whom it is named.</div> </div> </div> </div>Although the mechanical expression of this is a more firm thing of increasing mobility control in battle with things such as improved rushes and grapples, attaining flight and a special attack to blast people away from you; the literal transformation into an air dragon is kind of a consolidation of the preceding stuff in a particularly dramatic form. Really, it makes calling the armour &quot;Coil&quot; make more sense, and gives a clearer idea of the details. What <i>is</i> the elemental fury of an air dragon? It's being able to cling to an enemy that might be trying to evade and pushing off one you don't want present. There's even the basic quality of that in the armour's starting power of having no mobility penalty and being able to float on water, while dangerous fluids are kept at bay.<br /> <br /> So for Unison, the mechanical expression is how the base power is that one has the option to continuously shift the armour into forms with greater defensive benefits (at the cost of higher mote commitments, although with the option to shift back to a lower state to decrease the commitment), and then the powers are largely things that turn the character's relevant Intimacies into fighting bonuses or provide improvements to some defensive Solar Charms, some of which require the armour to be transformed to a specific level.<br /> <br /> These things lend themselves to how armour is distinguished from a weapon, if there's a certain more defensive quality or modification to the whole body. I think those details are useful to focus on, because having a broad array of Artifact categories limits the utility of a one-size-fits all description.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338575-brainstorming-an-artifact-\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022-suit-of-armor?p=1338628#post1338628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The first one, scope, increasing as you go from 3 to 5 dots means less that evocations become more and more powerful, and more that they become wider and grander in scope. So an artifact 3 weapon might fire a lightning bolt while an artifact 5 conjures an entire thunderstorm. Mechanically that lightning bolt may actually seal more damage and be technically more optimal for single combat, but that typhoon can wipe out the entire docks ward of a city, if not the entire thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>But then you get something like Stormcaller, where the city destroying stuff is building up whether you want it to or not and the underlying tension of the weapon is often relieving all of that pressure before it causes a lot of collateral damage by converting it into... a lightning bolt that is optimally targeted at a single opponent. Deliberate city destroying stuff is there, sure, but it's not the be-all end-all of the sword.<br /> <br /> Then you've got Soulfarer, which is all about slaying significant opponents to convert them into fuel for one's sorcery. Or Black Wind, which is all about finding specific perpetrators of wicked deeds and going after them; its mass destruction effect is concerned with taking down fortresses to get at the bad person hiding within them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The next, as mentioned above, is style. A lot of artifact 5 weapons and armor are almost like martial arts unto themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's more a description of Artifact 4 weapons. 5 tends to look more like a severely expressed core power that general combat and the further Evocations can stoke to greater intensity before they burst, or provide nuances and greater specificity to how that core power is applied.<br /> <br /> But that's the weapons. Armour on the whole is more understated, and I think we don't quite have enough level 5 armour to derive a pattern. Hmm, I want to look back and compare Mela's Coil to a bunch of the preceding armours and see if any distinct departure stands out. In any case, we certainly don't have any armours that imply doing something as externally focused as causing earthquakes; how does that help defend you?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lastly legend. Artifact 5s should be, probably, a big part of your PCs legend. As much as King Arthur and Thor are related to their weapons. So it should be a pretty big deal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Every Artifact is like that. If anything, the level 5 ones are actually often competing with their wielder for prominence, crowding them out a bit; the grandeur and intensity of them seems to make specific wielders fade a bit, compared with the highly personal qualities of Beloved Adorei, Pyre of Legions and whatever the name of the moonsilver panpipes of Nabira was. The most personal level 5 Artifact that isn't a warstrider thus far is probably Stormcaller, and that one's backstory is largely concerned with how it exerted a very strong influence in converting its first wielder into a terrifying monster.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T06:02:22-07:00","id":1338770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338575-brainstorming-an-artifact-\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022-suit-of-armor?p=1338767#post1338767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But then you get something like Stormcaller, where the city destroying stuff is building up whether you want it to or not and the underlying tension of the weapon is often relieving all of that pressure before it causes a lot of collateral damage by converting it into... a lightning bolt that is optimally targeted at a single opponent. Deliberate city destroying stuff is there, sure, but it's not the be-all end-all of the sword.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I probably should have used more varied examples. I meant that more as a guide that the awesome over the top power of Artifact 5 stuff when people hear about it might jump right to \u201cAwesome! Crazy legendary super powerful weapons? What about an evocation that gives double 7s on attack AND damage rolls for the scene!\u201d but no, that\u2019s not really how that power is expressed. Not that it CAN\u2019T make you more awesome in single combat, it just tends to not be so singularly focused on doing nothing but buffing your fighting docepools.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338575-brainstorming-an-artifact-\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022-suit-of-armor?p=1338767#post1338767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that's more a description of Artifact 4 weapons. 5 tends to look more like a severely expressed core power that general combat and the further Evocations can stoke to greater intensity before they burst, or provide nuances and greater specificity to how that core power is applied.<br /> <br /> But that's the weapons. Armour on the whole is more understated, and I think we don't quite have enough level 5 armour to derive a pattern. Hmm, I want to look back and compare Mela's Coil to a bunch of the preceding armours and see if any distinct departure stands out. In any case, we certainly don't have any armours that imply doing something as externally focused as causing earthquakes; how does that help defend you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Er...Mela\u2019s Coil lets you exhale a typhoon? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338575-brainstorming-an-artifact-\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022-suit-of-armor?p=1338767#post1338767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every Artifact is like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>They\u2019re supposed to be, but I find in practice they often aren\u2019t. A lot of people just take a daiklave for a daiklave and don\u2019t go into it. If you\u2019re taking a 5 dot one everyone involved should be making a concerted effort to make sure that this isn\u2019t just your shiny armor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T08:20:54-07:00","id":1338802,"title":"","content":"I've always struggled with high dot rating artifact armors. I've a playet that loves to play super tank to the point that he really want 5 dot heavy artifact armor, but building satisfying armor is really hard for that concept.<br /> <br /> What do you even do with the concept of super tank or immovable object that is fitting?<br /> So ideas of mechanics, gaining initiative when an enemy attack doesn't hurt the character. Enemies have penalties to leave close range of the Exalt. Counter attack used after being hit by a decisive attack. It creates a gambit that shatters mundane weapons and disarms artifact weapons. <br /> <br /> How do you scale it up to the really epic levels of 5 dot artifact?<br /> Allow defend other over a large area? Allow evocations to counts toward maintaining Agis of Invincible Might? Reduce or even remove the penalty associated with Adamantine Skin Technique and stopping uncountable damage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T10:36:40-07:00","id":1338834,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=1338833#post1338833\">Here</a>'s a concept for an &quot;Immovable Object&quot; Artifact.<br /> <br /> <i>Edit : made minor tweaks to the Evocations and added an appropriately epic capstone for a 5 dot artifact.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 10-01-2019, 03:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T11:06:20-07:00","id":1338842,"title":"","content":"This is tricky because the concept for the armour is the sort of thing that, to me a least lends itself to making 'basic' NPC antagonist equipment a little more interesting. <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <b>Immovable Mountain</b> (Attune):<br /> The mythic weight of Immovable Mountain works against those who would seek to push its bearer back. <br /> Attacks and effects that would force the wearer to move one or more range bands (such as Smashing Attacks) suffer a penalty to the roll equal to the armour's mobility penalty.<br /> <br /> As you can see it's quick and pretty simple with a visual component to it. I'd probably give it extra functionality verses grapples and some synergy with the full defence action.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> This is me shooting from the hip trying to make something I consider appropriate to that level.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <b>Insurmountable Arrogance</b> (Attune):<br /> Insurmountable Arrogance makes its wearer feel invincible, a feeling that's not misplaced if they master its powers.<br /> Whenever a Withering or Decisive Attack from a non-trivial opponent hits the Exalt but fails to deal damage to them, they gain a point of Hubris. The Exalt may gain up to (Essence + Stamina) Hubris during the combat, which is added directly to their soak rating but all points are lost if they should take Withering or Decisive damage. <br /> <br /> While Immovable Mountain was a useful piece of equipment with an added bonus against specific vectors of attack Insurmountable Arrogance is trying to dictate how you engage in combat and where you spend your xp (non-standard resources are good at this but should be used sparingly. You don't really want a character who has to seperately track *daiklave* points, *powerbow* points and *armour* points -that's the point where the system becomes a parody of itself). Later charms would offer new ways of gaining Hubris and exciting things to spend it on, assuming that the wearer didn\u2019t severely underestimate someone and die horribly before then.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T13:23:51-07:00","id":1338860,"title":"","content":"The ultimate expression of tanky armor IMO is All-Conquering Colossus. Yes, it's a warstrider, but that's about as tanky as it gets.<br /> <br /> In more seriousness, taking some of those evocations as guidelines and toning them down might be a good start. I'm a little rusty, but I'd almost say they're balanced as regular armor evocations if you drop all of the warstrider benefits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T16:36:24-07:00","id":1339079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338575-brainstorming-an-artifact-\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022-suit-of-armor?p=1338770#post1338770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, I probably should have used more varied examples. I meant that more as a guide that the awesome over the top power of Artifact 5 stuff when people hear about it might jump right to \u201cAwesome! Crazy legendary super powerful weapons? What about an evocation that gives double 7s on attack AND damage rolls for the scene!\u201d but no, that\u2019s not really how that power is expressed. Not that it CAN\u2019T make you more awesome in single combat, it just tends to not be so singularly focused on doing nothing but buffing your fighting docepools.<br /> <br /> <br /> Er...Mela\u2019s Coil lets you exhale a typhoon?<br /> <br /> <br /> They\u2019re supposed to be, but I find in practice they often aren\u2019t. A lot of people just take a daiklave for a daiklave and don\u2019t go into it. If you\u2019re taking a 5 dot one everyone involved should be making a concerted effort to make sure that this isn\u2019t just your shiny armor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those people are wasting the awesomeness of Artifact by not going into their crazy stories - i invest in control spell evocations just to have an excuse <i>for my PC's Wood Dragon Claw to turn into Exalted's version of the damn Hand of Vecna if my sorcerer ever dies</i>. If he survives long enough to learn Celestial Circle, i'll up the ante with Incomparable Body Arsenal for control spell, <i>so his corpse can become a diabolic suit of armor prone to messing up user's with my character's Intimacies</i>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I might also have a thing for making cronenbergian messes of charm, spell and artifact out of my characters, don't know. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-04-2019, 10:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T17:52:53-07:00","id":1339091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338575-brainstorming-an-artifact-\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022-suit-of-armor?p=1338770#post1338770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, I probably should have used more varied examples. I meant that more as a guide that the awesome over the top power of Artifact 5 stuff when people hear about it might jump right to \u201cAwesome! Crazy legendary super powerful weapons? What about an evocation that gives double 7s on attack AND damage rolls for the scene!\u201d but no, that\u2019s not really how that power is expressed. Not that it CAN\u2019T make you more awesome in single combat, it just tends to not be so singularly focused on doing nothing but buffing your fighting docepools.</div> </div> </div> </div>The middle ground is the Evocation that provides that dice bonus to a single attack and needs to expend something that the weapon has been building up every time it hit somebody.<br /> <br /> I can't speak to the hypothetical person who'll see Evocations in that manner, only my own experiences of how limited and obvious the upper end of magical items tends to be imagined as and how satisfying it is that Exalted does something more interesting. It just happens to be an interesting that doesn't work well with simple summaries, and so needs some detail.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Er...Mela\u2019s Coil lets you exhale a typhoon?</div> </div> </div> </div>A very small typhoon that pushes people away from you, keeping it within the armour's general defensive method of controlling mobility and position on the battlefield.<br /> <br /> That said, an earthquake probably isn't completely beyond the pale, but the Artifact needs to tell a credible story of how it got there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">They\u2019re supposed to be, but I find in practice they often aren\u2019t. A lot of people just take a daiklave for a daiklave and don\u2019t go into it.</div> </div> </div> </div>And they need other people to help broaden their horizons by persistently demanding that they actually look at the Artifacts.<br /> <br /> Honestly, don't go into it. &quot;Hmm, why does this daiklave keep taking off my health levels and setting me on fire? And why does the capstone provide me with an alternative to anything that gradually kills my character? Oh well! Ho him!&quot; Bah.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you\u2019re taking a 5 dot one everyone involved should be making a concerted effort to make sure that this isn\u2019t just your shiny armor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Artifact 5 is the point where it goes beyond being an instrument in one's legend into being a thing that is legendary in its own right, and part of one's renown will be the story of how one bent it to their will.<br /> <br /> Or perhaps it bent them. An unimaginative wielder might be at a bit of a disadvantage.<br /> <br /> Give them armour that ate all of its previous wearers, that might teach some respect. A bit on the nose to be sure, but apparently that's where we are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T18:47:52-07:00","id":1339097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338575-brainstorming-an-artifact-\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022-suit-of-armor?p=1339091#post1339091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The middle ground is the Evocation that provides that dice bonus to a single attack and needs to expend something that the weapon has been building up every time it hit somebody.<br /> <br /> I can't speak to the hypothetical person who'll see Evocations in that manner, only my own experiences of how limited and obvious the upper end of magical items tends to be imagined as and how satisfying it is that Exalted does something more interesting. It just happens to be an interesting that doesn't work well with simple summaries, and so needs some detail.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> A very small typhoon that pushes people away from you, keeping it within the armour's general defensive method of controlling mobility and position on the battlefield.<br /> <br /> That said, an earthquake probably isn't completely beyond the pale, but the Artifact needs to tell a credible story of how it got there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like the Jade Mountain Style charm (2e) that would absorb the power of an attack to transfer it to the ground, for example?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338575-brainstorming-an-artifact-\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022-suit-of-armor?p=1339091#post1339091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And they need other people to help broaden their horizons by persistently demanding that they actually look at the Artifacts.<br /> <br /> Honestly, don't go into it. &quot;Hmm, why does this daiklave keep taking off my health levels and setting me on fire? And why does the capstone provide me with an alternative to anything that gradually kills my character? Oh well! Ho him!&quot; Bah.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fortunately, not the case with anyone in the one group i have played 3e with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338575-brainstorming-an-artifact-\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022-suit-of-armor?p=1339091#post1339091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Artifact 5 is the point where it goes beyond being an instrument in one's legend into being a thing that is legendary in its own right, and part of one's renown will be the story of how one bent it to their will.<br /> <br /> Or perhaps it bent them. An unimaginative wielder might be at a bit of a disadvantage.<br /> <br /> Give them armour that ate all of its previous wearers, that might teach some respect. A bit on the nose to be sure, but apparently that's where we are.</div> </div> </div> </div>The sorcerer i mentioned in my previous post possibly has an Intimacy toward <i>becoming </i>that armor when he dies. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T19:02:32-07:00","id":1339098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338575-brainstorming-an-artifact-\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022-suit-of-armor?p=1339091#post1339091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A very small typhoon that pushes people away from you, keeping it within the armour's general defensive method of controlling mobility and position on the battlefield.<br /> <br /> That said, an earthquake probably isn't completely beyond the pale, but the Artifact needs to tell a credible story of how it got there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, to be specific my actual thinking behind the earthquake idea was an evocation that blocked decisive damage, shattering the earth under you in Close range, and an additional range band for each 5 damage negated. The idea being that if you're standing on a mountain and get struck with enough damage to break the mountain, then<i> the mountain</i> breaks first. Or something, I still haven't really thought it through.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338575-brainstorming-an-artifact-\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022-suit-of-armor?p=1339091#post1339091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And they need other people to help broaden their horizons by persistently demanding that they actually look at the Artifacts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's a little harsh, and also not quite exactly in line with the way Exalted presents artifacts. Marvel's version of Mjolnir is boarderline not even an artifact, but an Exaltation that empowers the worthy who wield it. The two's legend is inseparable, but quickly, and without looking it up, can you remember what Cathak Cainen's Direlance is called? Or Tepet Ejeva's plate armor? And when you read that first question did you instantly shake your head and ask yourself what I was talking about because he uses twin short daiklaves? Except he doesn't, because they're not twined, he has them attuned separately which means they're independent.<br /> <br /> Now what if I asked you what Elric's blade was called, or Arthas Menethil, or Link from Zelda. If you know the name Arthas Menethil, you know the name Frostmourne, it's almost impossible that you don't. There is no page long writeup for the Lich King that would ever leave out Frostmourne, but most of the Exalted character writeups don't even mention their artifacts once. It's not just players not understanding that every artifact should be as important to the wielder's story as Excalibur is to King Arthur.<br /> <br /> So if players want a daiklave and they put in half a thought maybe to what it's name is, if that, and then don't get into it I won't force them. They're free to go further if they want, and I encourage them to, of course. If they bought an artifact 5 hammer though? I will enforce they put a lot of thought into that, just like I wouldn't let a Solar start the game without telling me what cast they are, or a Dynast without telling me what house.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: wait a sec...are twin short daiklaves not attuned to as a pair? Was that 2e? That changes a lot if so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 10-03-2019, 12:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T21:49:10-07:00","id":1339123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338575-brainstorming-an-artifact-\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022-suit-of-armor?p=1339098#post1339098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, to be specific my actual thinking behind the earthquake idea was an evocation that blocked decisive damage, shattering the earth under you in Close range, and an additional range band for each 5 damage negated. The idea being that if you're standing on a mountain and get struck with enough damage to break the mountain, then<i> the mountain</i> breaks first. Or something, I still haven't really thought it through.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think that's a little harsh, and also not quite exactly in line with the way Exalted presents artifacts. Marvel's version of Mjolnir is boarderline not even an artifact, but an Exaltation that empowers the worthy who wield it. The two's legend is inseparable, but quickly, and without looking it up, can you remember what Cathak Cainen's Direlance is called? Or Tepet Ejeva's plate armor? And when you read that first question did you instantly shake your head and ask yourself what I was talking about because he uses twin short daiklaves? Except he doesn't, because they're not twined, he has them attuned separately which means they're independent.<br /> <br /> Now what if I asked you what Elric's blade was called, or Arthas Menethil, or Link from Zelda. If you know the name Arthas Menethil, you know the name Frostmourne, it's almost impossible that you don't. There is no page long writeup for the Lich King that would ever leave out Frostmourne, but most of the Exalted character writeups don't even mention their artifacts once. It's not just players not understanding that every artifact should be as important to the wielder's story as Excalibur is to King Arthur.<br /> <br /> So if players want a daiklave and they put in half a thought maybe to what it's name is, if that, and then don't get into it I won't force them. They're free to go further if they want, and I encourage them to, of course. If they bought an artifact 5 hammer though? I will enforce they put a lot of thought into that, just like I wouldn't let a Solar start the game without telling me what cast they are, or a Dynast without telling me what house.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: wait a sec...are twin short daiklaves not attuned to as a pair? Was that 2e? That changes a lot if so.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The ones you mentioned are not Artifact 5s though. Ejava's armor, Cainan's swords, etc are rare pieces of Exalted artifice, but they're not legendary in their own right; the ones that are, such as Mnemon's Emerald Thurible, are definitely always mentioned in their writeup and out of it too, and even then some of the Artifacts still get mentioned, such as Ejava's Thorn. Frostmourne, Mjolnir, the Master Blade, and so on are, in Exalted terms, either an Exigence in and of themselves that comes attached to the Artifact (Excalibur and its scabbard fit great here imo) or Artifact 5s that were just as legendary as their wielders (Gae Bolg, etc). I would, honestly, never really let a player just pick an Artifact weapon or armor only for the stats, it completely turns Artifacts into Sword +1s when that's exactly what they're not meant to be. At the very least I'd brew an Attunement bonus and an Evocation or two for it myself and discuss them with the player. Artifact 5s, doubly and triply so.<br /> <br /> Edit: Twin short daiklaves are attuned to as a pair, and so are other Artifacts that come paired, such as a hypothetical Excalibur and its scabbard, or a hypothetical Sword and Shield set, or the Blue Jade Devil Caster in Arms and its lost pair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T22:34:41-07:00","id":1339126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338575-brainstorming-an-artifact-\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022-suit-of-armor?p=1339098#post1339098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, to be specific my actual thinking behind the earthquake idea was an evocation that blocked decisive damage, shattering the earth under you in Close range, and an additional range band for each 5 damage negated. The idea being that if you're standing on a mountain and get struck with enough damage to break the mountain, then<i> the mountain</i> breaks first. Or something, I still haven't really thought it through.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rock Falls, Everybody Dies Inevitability. Sorry, i had to say it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But going back into the mountain theme, would not an avalanche make a better fit for imagery than an earthquake?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338575-brainstorming-an-artifact-\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022-suit-of-armor?p=1339098#post1339098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that's a little harsh, and also not quite exactly in line with the way Exalted presents artifacts. Marvel's version of Mjolnir is boarderline not even an artifact, but an Exaltation that empowers the worthy who wield it. The two's legend is inseparable, but quickly, and without looking it up, can you remember what Cathak Cainen's Direlance is called? Or Tepet Ejeva's plate armor? And when you read that first question did you instantly shake your head and ask yourself what I was talking about because he uses twin short daiklaves? Except he doesn't, because they're not twined, he has them attuned separately which means they're independent.<br /> <br /> Now what if I asked you what Elric's blade was called, or Arthas Menethil, or Link from Zelda. If you know the name Arthas Menethil, you know the name Frostmourne, it's almost impossible that you don't. There is no page long writeup for the Lich King that would ever leave out Frostmourne, but most of the Exalted character writeups don't even mention their artifacts once. It's not just players not understanding that every artifact should be as important to the wielder's story as Excalibur is to King Arthur.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the NPCs defense, how many of those already have 3e write-ups? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338575-brainstorming-an-artifact-\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022-suit-of-armor?p=1339098#post1339098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if players want a daiklave and they put in half a thought maybe to what it's name is, if that, and then don't get into it I won't force them. They're free to go further if they want, and I encourage them to, of course. If they bought an artifact 5 hammer though? I will enforce they put a lot of thought into that, just like I wouldn't let a Solar start the game without telling me what cast they are, or a Dynast without telling me what house.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: wait a sec...are twin short daiklaves not attuned to as a pair? Was that 2e? That changes a lot if so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Must admit i remember Cainan in art with a huge two-pronged Daiklave, not paired short daiklaves. That is something that always bothered me actually, as i have never seen a write-up for that blade, though i kind of expected it to be at least as storied as Relentless Wind, the blue jade daiklave Tepet Arada received as a gift/prize from one of his uncles for slaying the icewalker anathema warlord Jochim and once belonged to Tepet himself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-03-2019, 08:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T05:24:38-07:00","id":1339161,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> As an aside, irregardless of level, some artifacts did get a bit more legend through the editions than others.<br /> <br /> Like for example Dace's nameless Orichalcum Reaver Daiklave, inherited from his 1st Age incarnation, that by late 2nd ed, in Lords of Creation, we reacquainted with as Dawnlight, the blade that has served Contentious Sword and all of its many incarnations across history down to Aofe, a gloried solar general of the Primodial War, for whom it was gifted and forged by Kek'Tungssha, one of Autochton's souls itself.<br /> <br /> That is one subdued sample of giving some respectable history and subdued legend to what is an otherwise quite vanilla artifact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T05:27:22-07:00","id":1339162,"title":"","content":"IIRC, the blade had its name embossed on it; it wasn\u2019t nameless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T07:39:20-07:00","id":1339175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alistair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338575-brainstorming-an-artifact-\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022-suit-of-armor?p=1339123#post1339123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The ones you mentioned are not Artifact 5s though. Ejava's armor, Cainan's swords, etc are rare pieces of Exalted artifice, but they're not legendary in their own right; the ones that are, such as Mnemon's Emerald Thurible, are definitely always mentioned in their writeup and out of it too, and even then some of the Artifacts still get mentioned, such as Ejava's Thorn. Frostmourne, Mjolnir, the Master Blade, and so on are, in Exalted terms, either an Exigence in and of themselves that comes attached to the Artifact (Excalibur and its scabbard fit great here imo) or Artifact 5s that were just as legendary as their wielders (Gae Bolg, etc).</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, that\u2019s what I\u2019m saying. The artifact 3 weapons and armor used by those characters are not really in danger of matching the legend of their wielder, artifact 5s are and really demand to be incorporated as such.<br /> <br /> As for the artifact 3s, I usually ST for 4-5 people, almost all of them want artifact weapons and armor, and I\u2019ve never seen more than one or two at a time be interested in perusing evocations that hard. So for me to make up 8-9 unique backstories and evocation trees and keep them all in balance and in theme while doing everything else I\u2019m expected to do as an ST is just too much. You get an attunement bonus and that\u2019s it from me, unless you want to put forth some initiative and explore your items.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T09:52:19-07:00","id":1339207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338575-brainstorming-an-artifact-\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022-suit-of-armor?p=1339162#post1339162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC, the blade had its name embossed on it; it wasn\u2019t nameless.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hmm, could be, never looked into it. That said, was the name of Dawnlight ever given outside of such (possible but uncofirmed) easter egg for Old Realm buffs?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338575-brainstorming-an-artifact-\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022-suit-of-armor?p=1339175#post1339175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Right, that\u2019s what I\u2019m saying. The artifact 3 weapons and armor used by those characters are not really in danger of matching the legend of their wielder, artifact 5s are and really demand to be incorporated as such.<br /> <br /> As for the artifact 3s, I usually ST for 4-5 people, almost all of them want artifact weapons and armor, and I\u2019ve never seen more than one or two at a time be interested in perusing evocations that hard. So for me to make up 8-9 unique backstories and evocation trees and keep them all in balance and in theme while doing everything else I\u2019m expected to do as an ST is just too much. You get an attunement bonus and that\u2019s it from me, unless you want to put forth some initiative and explore your items.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed - as a ST i might point them in Arms' direction for basic baiting, i mean, evocative inspiration or maybe spin a bit of world-building or two from their artifacts to set up a springboard for them, but actual use and degree of investment is completely up to the players.<br /> <br /> Though i <i>might </i>throw the occasional savage adventurer out to KS them for that particular bit of mythic panoply.... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-03-2019, 01:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T10:21:21-07:00","id":1339213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338575-brainstorming-an-artifact-\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022-suit-of-armor?p=1339175#post1339175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Right, that\u2019s what I\u2019m saying. The artifact 3 weapons and armor used by those characters are not really in danger of matching the legend of their wielder, artifact 5s are and really demand to be incorporated as such.<br /> <br /> As for the artifact 3s, I usually ST for 4-5 people, almost all of them want artifact weapons and armor, and I\u2019ve never seen more than one or two at a time be interested in perusing evocations that hard. So for me to make up 8-9 unique backstories and evocation trees and keep them all in balance and in theme while doing everything else I\u2019m expected to do as an ST is just too much. You get an attunement bonus and that\u2019s it from me, unless you want to put forth some initiative and explore your items.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Different experiences - My players usually either don't pick an Artifact, or pick a published one, only in few cases asking me if something can be brewed. Even then, I wouldn't mind brewing more than a few, since I don't plan sessions that hard, and I'm pretty adamant about not letting Artifacts feel like stat boosters alone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T14:26:39-07:00","id":1339240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338575-brainstorming-an-artifact-\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022-suit-of-armor?p=1339098#post1339098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now what if I asked you what Elric's blade was called, or Arthas Menethil, or Link from Zelda. If you know the name Arthas Menethil, you know the name Frostmourne, it's almost impossible that you don't. There is no page long writeup for the Lich King that would ever leave out Frostmourne, but most of the Exalted character writeups don't even mention their artifacts once. It's not just players not understanding that every artifact should be as important to the wielder's story as Excalibur is to King Arthur.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that's a good comparison. Due to being a deconstruction of the big man theory coupled with how the default PC is immediately promoted to a significant positions of power, Exalted discourse has historically been contemptuous of its major NPCs. There is no Elric, Arthas or Link in Creation- just a PC shaped void.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T19:37:48-07:00","id":1339293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338575-brainstorming-an-artifact-\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022-suit-of-armor?p=1339240#post1339240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that's a good comparison. Due to being a deconstruction of the big man theory coupled with how the default PC is immediately promoted to a significant positions of power, Exalted discourse has historically been contemptuous of its major NPCs. There is no Elric, Arthas or Link in Creation- just a PC shaped void.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, the same strongly applies in Link/Hero of Time's case and incarnations through multiple eras, might said. So maybe not a good counterpoint either. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T04:40:17-07:00","id":1339332,"title":"","content":"I don't know much about Link and literally nothing about his sword, but assumed that LoveMonkey was posting in good faith when bringing him up in the same context as Elric and Arthas whose stories and relationships to their weapons I'm very much aware of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T07:01:45-07:00","id":1339364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338575-brainstorming-an-artifact-\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022-suit-of-armor?p=1339332#post1339332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know much about Link and literally nothing about his sword, but assumed that LoveMonkey was posting in good faith when bringing him up in the same context as Elric and Arthas whose stories and relationships to their weapons I'm very much aware of.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say he was indeed. My point would be more that the matter of a weapon's legend x its user can be a thorny one and sometimes the &quot;great man/woman&quot; overshadowing/contrasting to a present hero can be &quot;just&quot; a different facet/incarnation of yourself. We can see examples of this in Michael Moorcock's Eternal Champion cycle in its many iterations and IIRC correctly, Romance of the Three Kingdoms to a certain degree.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338575-brainstorming-an-artifact-\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022-suit-of-armor?p=1338860#post1338860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The ultimate expression of tanky armor IMO is All-Conquering Colossus. Yes, it's a warstrider, but that's about as tanky as it gets.<br /> <br /> In more seriousness, taking some of those evocations as guidelines and toning them down might be a good start. I'm a little rusty, but I'd almost say they're balanced as regular armor evocations if you drop all of the warstrider benefits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mela's Coil pinnacle charm has the wearer transforming into a towering dragon of blue jade as a synthesis of the exalt and the armor's spirit. Does not seem far-fetched, awesomely overkill that it could be, to use that as a springboard to make the jump from armor evocations to those of warstriders, at least to me.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hakkonen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338575-brainstorming-an-artifact-\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022-suit-of-armor#post1338575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of my players asked permission for a five-dot Artifact, and I granted it because it gives me a plot hook. The character is a Dynast's former retainer, who became a Dawn caste when he killed something he shouldn't have been able to kill (haven't settled on exactly what, yet). The Artifact is something he stole as he was fleeing the Dynast's service (the Dynast in question isn't a canon character, but I know who she is).</div> </div> </div> </div>A suit of armor is not exactly my definition of a quick grab while on the run, but well, it's Exalted so i guess fair is fair. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> OP, what can you tell us about this Dynast and his past connection - or lack of - with the stolen wonder? Have any inklings of the artifact's legend (or peculiar lack of), its past wearers or the previous holders of the PC's exaltation been introduced? Is the armor orichalcum, white jade, has a mix of both (gold on white or vice-versa can look nice indeed) or involves some more peculiar ingredients? Any inklings of the artifact's past, its past wearers or the previous holders of the PC's exaltation have been introduced?<br /> <br /> All of these can contribute ideas and imagery for you to play with in developing its personality and evocations, so feel free to throw in whatever comes to mind from your game as noteworthy or interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-04-2019, 10:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T06:39:48-07:00","id":1339582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338575-brainstorming-an-artifact-\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022-suit-of-armor?p=1339098#post1339098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that's a little harsh, and also not quite exactly in line with the way Exalted presents artifacts. Marvel's version of Mjolnir is boarderline not even an artifact, but an Exaltation that empowers the worthy who wield it. The two's legend is inseparable, but quickly, and without looking it up, can you remember what Cathak Cainen's Direlance is called? Or Tepet Ejeva's plate armor? And when you read that first question did you instantly shake your head and ask yourself what I was talking about because he uses twin short daiklaves? Except he doesn't, because they're not twined, he has them attuned separately which means they're independent.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really fault the way What Fire Has Wrought and Fangs at the Gate write the personal Artifacts of the sample NPCs because word count is at a premium and those character write-ups have higher priorities for what they do with their limited resources.<br /> <br /> I also don't fault those books because they still give distinct names to the possessions of those characters and part of the reason that the word count is limited is because it's directed towards dedicated Artifact write-ups, which strike me as the more significant place to take cues on how to observe Artifacts.<br /> <br /> I will also note that when Exalted in possession of Artifacts show up in Adversaries of the Righteous, their Artifacts are still given very brief write-ups and preliminary Evocations, which I find does a lot to link them together.<br /> <br /> How characters and their magical items are written in other settings in comparison to Exalted always needs to be mindful of how those stories are often not games, or at least ones in which the weapons are necessarily things that will drift among different owners.<br /> <br /> Anyway, armour. In Arms we've got three four-dot ones, two of which I can read as having a function of carrying a kind of heroic persona that the wearer can step into and harness for their own purposes, and the other providing specialized defence against a powerful and versatile danger. Looking at the powers of the two five-dot armours and thinking about what they have in common and how they could be a step up from that, I feel as though an idea for such Artifacts could be that they have a fully realized identity in their own right that the wearer is capable of hiding within or having take over a lot of the direction in their body. It's not necessarily outright transformation, although might be most likely where such is found.<br /> <br /> It still ends up being far too vague for my liking, but it's a start. <br /> <br /> For the idea brought up in the first post... I keep going back to a notion of harnessing Principles, but I don't recall that being what was suggested and I actually keep wondering about something more direct in its defences.<br /> <br /> Do we have any armours that build up and spend their own specialized resource like a lot of weapons have? I think that could be something to spread out some powerful Evocations for presenting a hardened defence; maybe some dramatic soak and Hardness benefits, but you need to have been spending several turns without changing position to build up the points for it.<br /> <br /> Also maybe something taking a few cues from Octavian's defensive Charms, he's got some pretty strong powers for the concept of being an unbowed, unbroken pillar of rock.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T10:07:18-07:00","id":1339625,"title":"","content":"Eyebright from Lunars has an Insight resource it can apply on Evocations and such. Three dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T10:11:17-07:00","id":1339626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alistair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338575-brainstorming-an-artifact-\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022-suit-of-armor?p=1339625#post1339625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eyebright from Lunars has an Insight resource it can apply on Evocations and such. Three dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not actually a resource that can be built or spent - its value is simply the highest relevant Intimacy you know about your target (2/3/4).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 10-05-2019, 01:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T10:19:21-07:00","id":1339627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338575-brainstorming-an-artifact-\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022-suit-of-armor?p=1339626#post1339626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not actually a resource that can be built or spent - its value is simply the highest relevant Intimacy you know about your target (2/3/4).</div> </div> </div> </div>Brilliant Sentinel absorbs your Anima?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-08T04:23:18-07:00","id":1340196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338575-brainstorming-an-artifact-\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022-suit-of-armor?p=1339364#post1339364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OP, what can you tell us about this Dynast and his past connection - or lack of - with the stolen wonder? Have any inklings of the artifact's legend (or peculiar lack of), its past wearers or the previous holders of the PC's exaltation been introduced? Is the armor orichalcum, white jade, has a mix of both (gold on white or vice-versa can look nice indeed) or involves some more peculiar ingredients? Any inklings of the artifact's past, its past wearers or the previous holders of the PC's exaltation have been introduced?<br /> <br /> All of these can contribute ideas and imagery for you to play with in developing its personality and evocations, so feel free to throw in whatever comes to mind from your game as noteworthy or interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hadn't really considered a prior connection; I had been thinking he grabbed it to aid in his escape from former comrades bent on butchering the Anathema in their midst. There's been no play as of yet; we've only done Session 0.<br /> <br /> I've bought Arms of the Chosen and I'm taking a break from reading it to write this; I may ask the player in question if he wants to dial back to a three-dot Artifact and spend those points elsewhere.<br /> <br /> Some ideas for Evocations, in no particular order:<br /> <br /> Rage-Inspiring Stance<br /> All visible enemies must succeed at a Willpower roll, difficulty of the armor wearer's Resolve, to attack anyone other than the wearer.<br /> <br /> War Invigorates the Warrior<br /> Every time the wearer takes damage from a withering attack, he regains a number of motes equal to the Initiative lost.<br /> <br /> Strength of the Base of the Pillar<br /> The wearer gains Essence automatic successes for resisting knockback, knockdown, or being thrown. (Side note: I may name the armor Usul.)<br /> <br /> Omphalos Does Not Move<br /> Possible capstone. The armor grows down into the earth, rooting the wearer in place; he cannot move while ODNM is active, but can magically strike and parry in all directions, and gains some kind of bonus to defense (Hardness? Not sure).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1856-hakkonen","name":"Hakkonen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-08T06:30:32-07:00","id":1340212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hakkonen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338575-brainstorming-an-artifact-\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022-suit-of-armor?p=1340196#post1340196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I hadn't really considered a prior connection; I had been thinking he grabbed it to aid in his escape from former comrades bent on butchering the Anathema in their midst. There's been no play as of yet; we've only done Session 0.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, grabbed where? In what kind of place were the PC and its dynast associates when he exalted and everything went pear-shaped? Was it the dynast's own home, a chapter house of the wild hunt, the mansion of a friend during a social visit or ball, a lost temple, palace, fortress, battlefield they were in the middle of exploring? Did the dynast - or someone conneected to it - know thaat armor was such a mighty wonder?<br /> <br /> Remember it's your <b>player</b>'s character in the first place - just asking him or her might bring up angles you would not expect (or are <i>all too expected</i>, depending on how used you are to the particular player <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />) but will certainly contribute to the whole process, as you ask each other questions and see what answers come out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hakkonen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338575-brainstorming-an-artifact-\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022-suit-of-armor?p=1340196#post1340196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've bought Arms of the Chosen and I'm taking a break from reading it to write this; I may ask the player in question if he wants to dial back to a three-dot Artifact and spend those points elsewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's up to you two. Discuss it and let him have a look at the book too before he decides. But remember he could get those two dots, diminish something else in one and end up buying <b>another </b>3-dot artifact...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hakkonen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338575-brainstorming-an-artifact-\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022-suit-of-armor?p=1340196#post1340196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some ideas for Evocations, in no particular order:<br /> <br /> Rage-Inspiring Stance<br /> All visible enemies must succeed at a Willpower roll, difficulty of the armor wearer's Resolve, to attack anyone other than the wearer.<br /> <br /> War Invigorates the Warrior<br /> Every time the wearer takes damage from a withering attack, he regains a number of motes equal to the Initiative lost.<br /> <br /> Strength of the Base of the Pillar<br /> The wearer gains Essence automatic successes for resisting knockback, knockdown, or being thrown. (Side note: I may name the armor Usul.)<br /> <br /> Omphalos Does Not Move<br /> Possible capstone. The armor grows down into the earth, rooting the wearer in place; he cannot move while ODNM is active, but can magically strike and parry in all directions, and gains some kind of bonus to defense (Hardness? Not sure).</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing that came to mind is that Solars <i><b>already </b></i>have natural charms that go well into the &quot;immovable object&quot; theme on their own. Depending if your player already intends to invest in resistance charms, you could make things much easier for your both by making evocations that spin from them, much like Irenio's Bell (Arms of Chosen, pg. 37-39) has a number that enhance performance (Singing Shield Technique for Battle Anthem (of the Solar Exalted), Solar Cantata, and Heroism-Encouraging Ballad) or melee (Resounding Thunder Deflection for Heavenly Guardian Defense) charms.<br /> <br /> Just a thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-08-2019, 09:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-08T08:19:53-07:00","id":1340237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hakkonen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338575-brainstorming-an-artifact-\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022-suit-of-armor?p=1340196#post1340196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Omphalos Does Not Move<br /> Possible capstone. The armor grows down into the earth, rooting the wearer in place; he cannot move while ODNM is active, but can magically strike and parry in all directions</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, direction isn't really something the combat system places any significance in; I don't recall anything that presumes you can ever be facing away from an enemy within range for purposes of attack or defence in any meaningful way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}